ot within the Statute of Frauds as a contract to answer for the duty of another. (g) A promise by an obligee’s agent that a purchaser of the obli- gee’s goods or services through the agent will pay the price of the goods to the obligee is not within the Statute of Frauds as a contract to an- swer for the duty of another. (h) A secondary obligor’s promise to the principal obligor to dis- charge a duty owed by the principal obligor to the obligee is not within the Statute of Frauds as a contract to answer for the duty of another. § 11 RESTATEMENT OF SURETYSHIP AND GUARANTY"